{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find \\(\\cos 1050^\\circ\\), we need to reduce the angle to an equivalent angle between \\(0^\\circ\\) and \\(360^\\circ\\). We do this by subtracting \\(360^\\circ\\) as many times as necessary until the angle is within the desired range.\n\nFirst, we calculate how many full rotations of \\(360^\\circ\\) are in \\(1050^\\circ\\):\n\\[ 1050^\\circ \\div 360^\\circ = 2.9167 \\]\nThis means that \\(1050^\\circ\\) is equivalent to \\(2\\) full rotations plus an additional angle. To find this additional angle, we subtract \\(2 \\times 360^\\circ\\) from \\(1050^\\circ\\):\n\\[ 1050^\\circ - 2 \\times 360^\\circ = 1050^\\circ - 720^\\circ = 330^\\circ \\]\nSo, \\(1050^\\circ\\) is equivalent to \\(330^\\circ\\). Now we need to find \\(\\cos 330^\\circ\\).\n\n","prefix_end":706,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,1124,11520,9407,220,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,59,701,582,1184,311,7949,279,9210,311,458,13578,9210,1948,17767,15,24884,43298,57758,323,17767,18,21,15,24884,43298,59,568,1205,653,419,553,32256,287,17767,18,21,15,24884,43298,57758,438,1657,3039,438,5871,3080,279,9210,374,2878,279,12685,2088,382,5338,11,582,11047,1246,1657,2480,69201,315,17767,18,21,15,24884,43298,57758,525,304,17767,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,59,982,78045,220,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,1124,611,220,18,21,15,24884,43298,284,220,17,13,24,16,21,22,1124,921,1986,3363,429,17767,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,57758,374,13578,311,17767,17,57758,2480,69201,5519,458,5107,9210,13,2014,1477,419,5107,9210,11,582,32256,17767,17,1124,15136,220,18,21,15,24884,43298,57758,504,17767,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,59,982,78045,220,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,481,220,17,1124,15136,220,18,21,15,24884,43298,284,220,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,481,220,22,17,15,24884,43298,284,220,18,18,15,24884,43298,1124,921,4416,11,17767,16,15,20,15,24884,43298,57758,374,13578,311,17767,18,18,15,2